3. Mods tandem needs at run time (not included, not modified)
-------------------------------------------------------------

Players install these themselves; tandem calls their public interfaces.

  RED4ext    (MIT, Octavian Dima)   loads tandem.dll
  redscript  (MIT, jac3km4)         compiles r6/scripts/tandem
  Codeware   (MIT, Pavel Siberx)    script API tandem's scripts call
  TweakXL    (MIT, Pavel Siberx)    loads r6/tweaks/tandem

Codeware's source (MIT, https://github.com/psiberx/cp2077-codeware) was
also read as a reference for how the engine works. Where tandem's own code
follows something it shows (a function's name for an address-library
hash, a structure's layout, the list of open-world quest phases, its hash
of a quest node path), the source file says so in a comment next to it,
and docs/research/engine-knowledge.md cites the file and commit. SharedPunk
(MIT, alphanin9) is cited there the same way.


4. What tandem does not contain
-------------------------------

No code in tandem comes from CyberpunkMP (Tilted Phoques), from Night City
Online, or from the campaign fork of CyberpunkMP. Those projects are
source-available under a licence that does not allow their code to be
reused, and none of it was copied, translated or adapted here.

What tandem did take from reading them is facts about the game: which
address-library hash names which function, measured structure offsets,
numbers, and what was observed to crash. Facts are not code. Each one is
written down with its source and how far it has been verified in
docs/research/ (engine-knowledge.md, nco-commits.md, campaign-fork.md),
and the implementation built on it is tandem's own.
